      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village is a National Historic Landmark District and the only one in Nebraska, recognized in 1985.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.boystown.org/nebraska/about",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Boys Town houses the national headquarters, a museum called The Hall of History, and a post office—all within the historic village.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boys_Town%2C_Nebraska",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The village earned repeated honors as one of the \"100 Best Communities for Young People\" by America's Promise Alliance.",
